
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Device1 as Device 1<br/>cartVersion: 5
  actor Device2 as Device 2<br/>cartVersion: 5
  participant Order as Order<br/>cart version check
  participant Redis as Redis<br/>cart state + version

  Device1->>Order: Add item to cart<br/>expected version: 5
  Order->>Redis: Compare and update
  Redis->>Redis: Version matches<br/>apply change v5 → v6
  Redis-->>Order: Updated cart v6
  Order-->>Device1: Success, cart v6

  Device2->>Order: Add different item<br/>expected version: 5 (stale)
  Order->>Redis: Compare and update
  Redis-->>Order: Version mismatch<br/>expected 5, actual 6
  Order-->>Device2: 409 CONFLICT<br/>+ current cart v6

  Device2->>Order: Refetch cart state
  Order->>Redis: Read current cart
  Redis-->>Order: Cart v6
  Order-->>Device2: Cart v6

  Device2->>Order: Retry with version 6
  Order->>Redis: Compare and update
  Redis->>Redis: Version matches<br/>apply change v6 → v7
  Redis-->>Order: Updated cart v7
  Order-->>Device2: Success, cart v7

  Note over Order,Redis: Optimistic version prevents lost updates.<br/>Client must retry with the version received from the conflict response.
